flowchart TB
accTitle: Structured simulator rollouts remain isolated planning branches
accDescr: A versioned root snapshot seeds a planning state. Candidate commands are applied by the deterministic supply-chain simulator to isolated branch snapshots. The rollout is a structured domain transition, not a model-generated imagined outcome and not environmental feedback. Candidate branches are replayed and evaluated; a separate later grounding path may change the current world after the required authorization and dispatch.

    ROOT[Root simulated snapshot<br/>version v]
    ROOT --> S0[Planning root state]
    S0 --> C1[Candidate action A]
    S0 --> C2[Candidate action B]
    C1 --> SIM1[Deterministic simulator<br/>isolated branch A]
    C2 --> SIM2[Deterministic simulator<br/>isolated branch B]
    SIM1 --> E1[Replay and evaluate]
    SIM2 --> E2[Replay and evaluate]
    E1 --> CAND[Auditable plan candidate]
    E2 --> CAND
    CAND --> AUTH[Later authorization<br/>and dispatch]
    AUTH --> WORLD[Current simulated world<br/>may advance]
